%erg 0.1
Title: Skip PR loop for erg-only branches
Created: 2026-05-14
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-05-14T09:30Z MinhHaDuong created

--- body ---
## Context
When a branch contains only `.erg` file changes (ticket creates, closes, log
entries), the full PR + CI-wait loop is pure overhead — there is no code risk
and no review value. A fast-forward push directly to main is the right move.

## Actions
1. In `ticket-close` skill: after staging the closed ticket move, check whether
   the branch diff (vs main) touches any file outside `tickets/`. If not, push
   directly to `origin/main` via `git push origin HEAD:main` instead of opening
   a PR.
2. In `erg-pr-merge` (if it exists as a separate skill/script): skip the CI wait
   when `git diff origin/main...HEAD -- . ':(exclude)tickets/' | wc -c` is 0.
3. Add a safety guard: if the direct push fails (e.g. non-fast-forward), fall
   back to the normal PR path.

## Test
Create a branch with only a `.erg` file change. Run `ticket-close`. Verify no
PR is created and the commit lands on main directly.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `ticket-close` detects erg-only branches and pushes directly to main
- [ ] Non-erg changes still go through the normal PR path
- [ ] Fast-forward failure falls back to PR path without error
- [ ] `make check` (or equivalent) passes
